SDL2-for-Pascal — the fourth platform arm, in the copy Fairtris 2 vendors.
Applies to a copy of the game's `source/` tree with `patch -p1`, from the
game's top directory. Never to the checkout itself.

SDL2-for-Pascal is the Pascal translation of SDL2's headers. Fairtris 2
carries its own copy in `source/sdl/`. Every routine in it is declared
`external SDL_LibName` (or IMG_LibName, MIX_LibName), and each of those
constants is declared in three arms: Windows, Unix, and Classic Mac OS. A
target matching none of them leaves the constant undeclared, and the compile
stops at the first declaration that uses it, saying `identifier not found` —
naming neither the constant's purpose nor the platform. This adds a fourth
arm for circlesdl2, and a `uses ctypes` the Unix arm gets from UnixType.

The library name is never opened and never looked up. There is no loader on
this machine: every SDL2 entry point is resolved when the host kernel's
Circle build links libSDL2-<board>.a, exactly as a C caller's is. The
constants exist only so the `external` clauses have something to name.

Nothing is removed and nothing is stubbed. The binding still declares the
whole of SDL2; Free Pascal emits a reference only where a call is written,
so a declaration nobody calls never reaches the linker. That is what lets a
game be ported by relinking it.

The other arms cannot be used instead, and circle-libfpc's own
patches/README.md records why each was tried and rejected: -dUNIX and
-dWINDOWS make the binding's interface use units that do not exist on this
target, and -dMACOS compiles but renames every entry point with a leading
underscore, so the failure arrives at the link a long way from its cause.
--- a/source/sdl/sdl2.pas
+++ b/source/sdl/sdl2.pas
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@
       UnixType;
   {$ENDIF}
 
+  {$IFDEF CIRCLESDL2}
+    uses
+      ctypes;
+  {$ENDIF}
+
 const
 
   {$IFDEF WINDOWS}
@@ -120,7 +125,11 @@
     {$ENDIF}
   {$ENDIF}
 
+  {$IFDEF CIRCLESDL2}
+    SDL_LibName = 'SDL2';
+  {$ENDIF}
 
+
 {$DEFINE WANT_CWCHAR_T}
 {$I ctypes.inc}                  // C data types
 
--- a/source/sdl/sdl2_image.pas
+++ b/source/sdl/sdl2_image.pas
@@ -63,6 +63,10 @@
     {$ENDIF}
   {$ENDIF}
 
+  {$IFDEF CIRCLESDL2}
+    IMG_LibName = 'SDL2';
+  {$ENDIF}
+
   {* Printable format: "%d.%d.%d", MAJOR, MINOR, PATCHLEVEL *}
   SDL_IMAGE_MAJOR_VERSION = 2;
   SDL_IMAGE_MINOR_VERSION = 0;
--- a/source/sdl/sdl2_mixer.pas
+++ b/source/sdl/sdl2_mixer.pas
@@ -55,6 +55,10 @@
     {$IFDEF FPC}
       {$linklib libSDL2_mixer}
     {$ENDIF}
+  {$ENDIF}
+
+  {$IFDEF CIRCLESDL2}
+    MIX_LibName = 'SDL2';
   {$ENDIF}
 
   {* Printable format: "%d.%d.%d", MAJOR, MINOR, PATCHLEVEL *}
